        supported: true,
        description: "Play one card to the current trick. Must follow suit if possible. If void in the led suit you may play any card; the first such play establishes that card's suit as trumps for the rest of the hand. Once trumps are set, you must follow suit or play a trump (in Swiss Jass you may trump even when holding the led suit). If unable to follow and not trumping, you may play any card. The Puur (Under of trumps) need not be played when trumps are led and it is your only trump.",
